1
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:02,340
Hello there!

2
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:10,530
Howdy!

3
00:00:10,613 --> 00:00:12,580
I'm Hatake, Noko Hatake.

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,197
Oh, but everyone calls
me field these days.

5
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:17,597
I was just a regular old student in Japan,

6
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:20,504
then all of a sudden,
that anime thing happened.

7
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:24,000
I was reborn in another world,
as a field of all things.

8
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:27,457
I'm 100 meters long on each
side and 10 meters deep.

9
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:30,920
Now then, let me introduce
you to my lovable family.

10
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:35,037
See that sleek fellow with black
feathers, three eyes, and three legs?

11
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:37,780
That's Kuroyata, the ruler of the skies.

12
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:43,720
The party animal with a cute horn who
loves rushing into danger. Bow time!

13
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:48,560
A sluffle of sharp ears and fuzzy faces.

14
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,460
Meet the dad, Usata.

15
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:54,400
Mama Usarion and kiddos,
Usarion and Usapi.

16
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:56,897
That's my fam for ya.

17
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:58,640
But wait, there's more!

18
00:00:58,940 --> 00:01:01,620
This grateful ground has close pals.

19
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:05,320
Kikuyu, the recently grown-up snow fairy.

20
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:08,257
I mean, we're so close,
she's basically family.

21
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:11,420
She's my interpreter,
so I owe her big time.

22
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:16,620
And someone whose captivating eyes
almost made me accidentally fall in love.

23
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:21,720
The lovely head of the fortified city
with a truly bewitching gaze, Jessica.

24
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:25,597
He's sharp as a tack and looks
like a standard-issue butler.

25
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:26,520
Stick.

26
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:30,537
Expressionless, potty-mouthed,
and so gosh-darn fond of animals,

27
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:33,677
she has a tendency to gush over
them to an uncomfortable degree.

28
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:34,680
It's murder.

29
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:39,417
She dresses like a knight,
but she's actually a princess.

30
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,537
Though she seems like
the epitome of capable,

31
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:43,697
she's more of a hot mess than you think.

32
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:44,760
It's Hayachi.

33
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:48,477
Qyoehkotek is the vampire
necromancer with an impossible

34
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:51,795
name who runs hot and cold
and is the left-leg general.

35
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:55,057
Those awesome peeps are my support system.

36
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:59,697
Thanks to them, my time as a sentient field
has been peaceful and pleasantly boring.

37
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:03,309
Oh, except for that one time I
fought the Demon Lord's army.

38
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:07,377
After a fierce duel with the Demon
Lord's former left-legged general,

39
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:11,777
my consciousness was interrupted, and
I lost my sense of self for a while.

40
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:14,637
The days melted away as I
drifted through darkness.

41
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:19,360
I nearly went mad from the loneliness,
until one day, out of nowhere,

42
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:20,898
the light returned.

43
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:26,840
The darkness was gone, replaced by my
friends and family in a world of light.

44
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:29,733
Actually, that was just a few weeks ago.

45
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,760
While I was spiraling into madness,

46
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:37,237
Qyoehkotek was spreading my top-tier
veggie seeds and seedlings around.

47
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:41,555
That fixed the little starvation issue
plaguing the Demon Lord's domain.

48
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:44,397
This made the Demon Lord pro-field,

49
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:47,657
and I was soon invited to his
castle so we could begin peace

50
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:51,446
negotiations between his Demon
forces and the fortified city.

51
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,517
Shui, now you're up to speed.

52
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:57,317
Silly field, you've been monologuing
for almost three minutes straight.

53
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,257
Whatever am I going to do with you?

54
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:00,280
Kiku, you!

55
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:03,972
I can't believe you've blossomed
into such a beauty queen!

56
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:09,177
That's sweet of you to say, though I'm
unaccustomed to receiving such compliments.

57
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:11,077
Piece, I totally forgot.

58
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,977
She can hear my innermost thoughts.

59
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:15,497
What's with all the
shameless flirting over here?

60
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:18,933
And more importantly, why
isn't any of it directed at me?

61
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,030
Qyoehkotek.

62
00:03:20,113 --> 00:03:22,217
Even though she saved the
demon realm from famine

63
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:25,037
and became the new
left-legged general to boot,

64
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:28,767
that overachiever still spends
her days tending to my gardens.

65
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:33,400
But on a positive note, you've really
gotten the hang of moving around.

66
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:36,327
I can hardly feel the
ground shaking anymore.

67
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,682
You're doing so much better now.

68
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,230
Thanks!

69
00:03:40,313 --> 00:03:41,357
I've been practicing.

70
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:44,911
These fieldy feet are taking
us to the demon lord's castle!

71
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:53,530
Whaaaaaa!

72
00:03:53,613 --> 00:03:55,437
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box.

73
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:57,757
But inside, I've still got a human soul!

74
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,257
In this new world of wonders,

75
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:02,857
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner, Lamas!

76
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:04,940
The name's Boxxo. Hello there!

77
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:06,740
That means yes, by the way.

78
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:16,737
Take my turn.

79
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:18,180
Go, go, go!

80
00:04:29,473 --> 00:04:30,303
How do you feel?

81
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,678
God, no, that's me.

82
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:24,080
I'm beyond stoked to visit
the Demon Lord's castle.

83
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:26,340
He's a surprisingly decent person.

84
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:29,097
We've spoken a handful
of times at this point.

85
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:30,560
I kind of like the guy.

86
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,712
The sun barely shines in the Demon Realm.

87
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:36,409
It's a barren place
where crops won't grow.

88
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:39,637
Till now, I've been working
my bountiful booty off.

89
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,237
To modify the veggies I produce?

90
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:44,020
into hardy, drought-resistant cultivars.

91
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:47,157
They're spreading like wildfire
around the demon realm,

92
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:49,817
making mincemeat of that
nasty food shortage.

93
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:53,677
Now that we're not desperate for
resources, we've even stopped warmongering.

94
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:56,397
A happy side effect is that
everyone in the demon realm

95
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:59,337
has been treating me like
some kind of heroic hotshot.

96
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:01,680
Me, a humble field!

97
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,917
You know I don't like it
when you're overly modest.

98
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,777
Why shouldn't everyone be in awe of the

99
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:09,457
person who made those
life-saving vegetables?

100
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:11,380
You're so nice, Kikuyu.

101
00:06:11,940 --> 00:06:14,137
By the way, I was hoping
you could tell me?

102
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,877
About that other Japanese guy you met?

103
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:19,019
who was reborn as an inanimate
object in this world.

104
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:20,920
Sure, I'd be happy to.

105
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,430
Wild.

106
00:06:22,513 --> 00:06:26,417
What are the odds that another Japanese
dude would be reincarnated here?

107
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:30,980
He was reborn as a vending machine and
now wanders the dungeon. Righteous!

108
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:33,415
That's even random by anime standards!

109
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:36,137
Er, says I, the guy who
was reborn as a field.

110
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:37,140
That's right.

111
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:40,017
I clearly remember him saying
he was a vending machine.

112
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,817
He has the ability to transform
into different types of

113
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:46,397
vending machine at will and
dispense the associated products.

114
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:49,117
It sounds like he helped
you out of a ripe pickle.

115
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:53,677
So once we settle our problems here, I'm
thinking we should go and return the favor.

116
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:54,590
You know,

117
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:58,857
I still can't believe the left-armed
general's been plotting in the dungeon.

118
00:06:58,940 --> 00:06:59,770
Don't worry.

119
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:02,557
No matter what happens, I'm
staying right by your side.

120
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,600
There's just one little problem.

121
00:07:04,860 --> 00:07:08,497
Can I ask Qyoehkotek for help when
she's the new left-legged general?

122
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:11,217
Guess I'll have to shoot my
shot and see what happens.

123
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,130
No stalling.

124
00:07:12,213 --> 00:07:13,340
It's now or never.

125
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:16,580
Yeah, of course I'll stick around.

126
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,531
The Demon Lord is ultimately just my boss.

127
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:23,937
I haven't forgotten, you're the one who
saved my village in this entire realm.

128
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,577
But don't get the wrong idea.

129
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:28,337
It's not like I have a secret
crush on you or anything.

130
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,277
I'm just paying you back, that's all.

131
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:32,400
I love a good tsundere trope.

132
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,657
But in all seriousness,

133
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:37,037
I'll assume she's being honest about
not crushing on a large clump of dirt.

134
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:40,197
I'll just count myself lucky
to have such a reliable ally.

135
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:43,157
Her ability to control the
dead is necromantastic,

136
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,457
and the two of us have amazing chemistry.

137
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:48,220
If you want good
chemistry, look no further.

138
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:51,340
True, it do be that way.

139
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,340
It's the Demon Lord's castle.

140
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:06,420
The head honcho, looking
effortlessly suave as always.

141
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,740
He's buff and handsome,
not to mention charismatic.

142
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:13,445
On paper, it looks like
an overwhelming defeat.

143
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,340
Not today, demon lord.

144
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:19,280
Those buff arms can't produce
life-saving sustenance. See that?

145
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:21,340
I'm not even a tiny bit jealous.

146
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:24,237
Alrighty, got that out of my system.

147
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:26,849
That elder gent is the
right-armed general.

148
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:30,717
He strikes me as a dandy who's
50 but still fit as a fiddle.

149
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:34,520
If I'd continued aging like a
human, I'd probably look similar.

150
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:36,420
Who am I kidding?

151
00:08:36,740 --> 00:08:39,152
I didn't even look that good in my prime.

152
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:50,500
Pardon me for literally treading on you.

153
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,271
It's finally time for the moment of truth.

154
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:56,579
Here's hoping our peace
negotiations go as expected.

155
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:01,880
I have not seen you in a long while

156
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:06,800
Or you, my faithful left-legged
general It's good to see you, sire

157
00:09:09,620 --> 00:09:11,700
Long time Yes,

158
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:16,840
too long And drop the formalities,
Qyoehkotek Right, general?

159
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:19,557
Since our realm of Lord
Fiela did have gratitude.

160
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:21,317
It seems he deserves an exception.

161
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,377
Oh.

162
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:23,480
By the way.

163
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:26,117
I feel a bit dehydrated.

164
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:29,435
I wish I could wet my tongue
with something refreshing.

165
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:33,120
I know exactly what he wants,
and I know, he knows, I know.

166
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,435
Please help yourself.

167
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,180
Today's juice.

168
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:41,399
It's from freshly squeezed Barrens.

169
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,740
Lovely. I accept.

170
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:52,360
My lord!

171
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,700
Was it poisoned?

172
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,460
Calm yourself.

173
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:59,400
It was so delectable, I felt woozy.

174
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:02,680
You simply must have a swig. Enjoy!

175
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:21,920
Impressive recovery!

176
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,595
You've earned yourself a little treat!

177
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,580
Oh, so shiny! Ha!

178
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:37,233
Even the Demon Lord is no
match for a juicy fruit basket!

179
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,577
You're in good spirits.

180
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:43,490
Having fun?

181
00:10:43,573 --> 00:10:45,680
Yep, I'm living my best life. Mm.

182
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:50,380
Ha ha ha ha ha!

183
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,960
Ha ha ha ha ha!

184
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:55,600
Ha ha ha ha! Incredible!

185
00:10:57,320 --> 00:11:00,000
It's possible I overdid it on the umami.

186
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:02,580
Wanna save peace talks for tomorrow?

187
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:05,138
No, I'd like to get this done today.

188
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:08,130
There!

189
00:11:08,213 --> 00:11:12,494
Now the Demon Lord's army will finally
stop attacking the fortified city.

190
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:16,360
Oh, Usapi and Usarion!

191
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,935
Do you have something for me in there?

192
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:20,780
This is unexpected.

193
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:25,377
I thought the Usapta family was off
investigating the murderous forest with Hayachi.

194
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:26,380
Let's see.

195
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:29,437
The left-armed general is...

196
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:33,480
That fiend is pulling shenanigans
during pace negotiations!

197
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:35,120
You seem perturbed.

198
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,670
Interesting.

199
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:42,217
He stole the dungeon's power and now
he's marching on the fortified city.

200
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,130
See this?

201
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:47,304
Well now, the left-armed general
really outdid himself this time.

202
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,320
Was this on your orders?

203
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:51,280
Of course it wasn't.

204
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,377
That wayward general did
this of his own volition.

205
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:57,717
I've known that he was capable
of treachery for a while now,

206
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:01,117
but attaining the dungeon's
power must have gone to his head.

207
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:05,080
Then it's no problem if I
crush him? Left arm? Do it.

208
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:06,200
I don't mind.

209
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:09,386
I'll even send reinforcements
to help you out.

210
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:13,100
If I may, I would like
to undertake that duty.

211
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:16,360
That's what I had in
mind as well. Go ahead.

212
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:18,460
Sire, I won't fail you.

213
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:23,057
We wrote a letter about
friending up the Demon Lord,

214
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:26,964
and then gave it to Kuroyata to
deliver it to the fortified city.

215
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:29,397
We left the Demon Lord's realm and should

216
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:32,009
be reaching the city
ourselves before long.

217
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:33,430
Okay,

218
00:12:33,513 --> 00:12:38,304
once we make it there, I'll have to request
to speak with Lady Jessica post-haste.

219
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:39,420
It's just,

220
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:44,252
the moment we lock eyes, I might go
into a trance and forget why I'm there!

221
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:50,597
You seem especially giddy when you
speak with Lady Jessica, am I wrong?

222
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:52,257
That observation is accurate.

223
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:54,617
who doesn't act that way in my presence.

224
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:58,053
I don't have the foggiest idea
what you're talking about.

225
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:01,920
The ladies in my life are
having a House fit. The cure?

226
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,780
Some fresh Utsugas.

227
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:07,237
Hey, you can't buy our
forgiveness, so don't even try it.

228
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,620
Yeah, she's right.

229
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:12,440
You can't tempt a woman with
fruit, you snake. Come on, now.

230
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:14,057
You know you want some of this.

231
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:15,669
You can't fool me, ladies.

232
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:17,274
Give in to temptation.

233
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:19,800
Field, stop being so creepy. Creepy?

234
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:21,844
What was that dirtbag thinking?

235
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:23,170
I'll tell you.

236
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:29,600
A few stray thoughts and
they're teaming up against me.

237
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:41,280
We love real!

238
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,140
Welcome back, Guardian.

239
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:50,420
It's lovely to see you.

240
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:52,540
Good to be back.

241
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:54,800
I'm glad you seem to be thriving.

242
00:13:57,260 --> 00:14:00,201
I'm supposed to be a field,
not an active volcano!

243
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:01,640
Be strong.

244
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:02,897
Jessica's a dude.

245
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:03,980
A bodacious dude.

246
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:06,256
But my brain must master my hormones!

247
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,860
I'll just say this once.

248
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,097
You're making Field uncomfortable.

249
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:13,457
Please take your hands off him at once.

250
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:16,377
Are you truly uncomfortable,
my precious guardian?

251
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:19,257
Is it really so wrong for
me to stroke you like this?

252
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:21,540
I may be afield, but I'm still a man.

253
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:24,877
I can't say yes when those
dazzling eyes are staring at me.

254
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,019
Welp, I guess I'll plead the fifth.

255
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,680
Answer already. You're waiting.

256
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:32,797
It makes you uncomfortable,
doesn't it, field?

257
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,710
Yay, yay!

258
00:14:33,793 --> 00:14:35,957
The path of retreat has been blockaded!

259
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:37,687
Requesting immediate backup!

260
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,760
Dang, looks like I'm on my own.

261
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,560
Alright, let's clear things up, shall we?

262
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:50,157
If you had to decide between the
three of us, who would you choose?

263
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:52,377
That's a rather intriguing proposition.

264
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:55,337
I have absolutely no
romantic interest in you,

265
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:58,857
but if you insist on being with me,
I'll give it serious consideration.

266
00:14:58,940 --> 00:14:59,770
No promises.

267
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:03,577
If you choose me, I swear I'll
devote my life to making you happy.

268
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:04,490
Whoa!

269
00:15:04,573 --> 00:15:06,280
Quick reminder, I'm a field?

270
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:09,437
Last time I checked, fields
don't have harem battles?

271
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,350
Answer.

272
00:15:10,433 --> 00:15:11,957
Did you all forget your crazy pills?

273
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:15,277
I'm a field! Pack dirt! Whip chow! Answer!

274
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,120
Emergency Destruction!

275
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,737
These babies are all yours if you help me

276
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:24,349
think of a plan to be
the Left Arm General.

277
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,300
So be it.

278
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:29,854
We shall indulge in those
Utsukas after our War Council.

279
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:30,910
Agreed.

280
00:15:30,993 --> 00:15:34,040
Looks like I narrowly
avoided disaster. But wait!

281
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:36,097
The fortified city's under attack!

282
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:38,957
So shouldn't we have started
the War Council ASAP?

283
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,760
Is this charade finally over?

284
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:43,877
If you're finished, we should
begin the War Council at once.

285
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:46,460
We're fast approaching the final showdown!

286
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,177
Woo-wee!

287
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:54,077
Getting to fill up our bellies with piping

288
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:56,748
out food on the
battlefield's a real luxury!

289
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,160
It truly is.

290
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,420
Hey, Hulemy!

291
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,137
You should eat something!

292
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:03,632
Just as soon as I finish installing this.

293
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:07,897
Hulamy's upgrading the Cap's wagon so
we can hitch it to my pimped-out pickup.

294
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:10,333
As the saying goes, waste not, want not.

295
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:14,040
It just had to rain, didn't it?

296
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,940
I was almost finished, too.

297
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:18,700
Rain, I'm afraid you've met your match.

298
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:23,080
Behold the glory of
poncho vending machines.

299
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,654
They're for water rides in theme parks.

300
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,000
This is perfect, Boxo.

301
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:31,677
We built a shelter from
the concrete blocks I

302
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,077
can plop out when I'm a
giant vending machine.

303
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:38,037
The injured hunters can rest there
safely while we rush to find our friends.

304
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,885
There isn't a moment to waste.

305
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:44,857
So if we keep on chugging along this way,
we'll wind up in the Massacre Forest?

306
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:46,157
The Murderous Forest.

307
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,534
And I'm pretty sure we're almost there.

308
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:51,220
The forest!

309
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:57,077
What happens next will depend
on what caused this destruction.

310
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,880
The monsters or our friends.

311
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,140
It's a mystery.

312
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:04,517
The ones who went ahead of us were
Director Bear, Heavy, Karios and Gores.

313
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:07,057
Oh, and Mishuel with his
big old dragon sword.

314
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:09,417
Yeah, I bet it was that last one I said.

315
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:10,330
Good thinking.

316
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:11,302
It makes sense.

317
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:13,618
Maybe he was slowing down the enemy.

318
00:17:14,140 --> 00:17:18,022
Mishuel, did you stay behind all
alone to keep the enemy occupied?

319
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:20,340
Master Boxxo!

320
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:21,477
Oh, there he is.

321
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,160
Master Boxxo!

322
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:24,780
Hello, Master.

323
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,377
I'm so happy you're safe.

324
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:29,300
I swear, I never stop believing in you.

325
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:33,140
Good work, Appalentant. Thanks, man.

326
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:36,637
Were you the ones who torched the forest?

327
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:37,737
I'm afraid so.

328
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:40,920
We had intended to buy
time via well-placed traps,

329
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:44,200
but then they were all
trampled by a giant monster.

330
00:17:44,460 --> 00:17:47,517
Sadly, we had no choice but
to set the forest ablaze.

331
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:50,617
Uh, Mishuel, is that the royal
we or is someone with you?

332
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:55,641
My sister and her adorable friend showed
up just in the nick of time to help me out.

333
00:17:56,380 --> 00:17:58,157
Hayachi! Usata! Usarion!

334
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,475
You can come out now!

335
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:03,337
It's a pleasure to finally meet you.

336
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:06,397
I'm exceedingly grateful for everything
you've done for my little brother.

337
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:08,068
These are my Essig friends.

338
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:10,380
Their names are Usata and Usarion.

339
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:12,680
I owe those two my life.

340
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:16,237
They rescued me after I happened
upon the Four-Fingered General.

341
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:18,614
Their swordsmanship is truly unmatched.

342
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:19,940
Or earmanship.

343
00:18:20,980 --> 00:18:21,810
Amazing.

344
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:23,881
I can sense their great strength.

345
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,740
Form change!

346
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,560
Our posse's growing.

347
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:30,393
One truck's not enough.

348
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,441
And two's better than one anyway.

349
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,150
What?

350
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:35,517
The Netherlord's gone rogue?

351
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:38,894
So he's not doing the bidding
of the Demon Lord anymore?

352
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:39,882
That's correct.

353
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:42,817
The Netherlord used to
rule over the Demon Realm,

354
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:47,135
but he lost his throne to the current
Demon Lord and became his subject.

355
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:48,440
Didn't know that.

356
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:52,037
Sounds like a solid motivation
for betraying the Demon Lord.

357
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:56,061
On the upside, now we only have to
go ham on the Netherlord's army.

358
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,945
Our odds of winning this
just got a lot better.

359
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:03,557
Even still, it would be best if we could
join forces with the fortified city.

360
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:06,758
Too bad we have no way of
getting in touch with them.

361
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:07,710
Hmm.

362
00:19:07,793 --> 00:19:08,623
I miss email.

363
00:19:08,706 --> 00:19:10,040
Look, up in the air.

364
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:11,720
It's Kroyata!

365
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:15,960
Hello, old friend.

366
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:17,137
What brings you here?

367
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:18,717
I'm surprised you found us.

368
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:19,630
How's Kikoyu?

369
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,590
Oh, hey.

370
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:23,584
He's got a little birdie pouch.

371
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,624
It must be some kind of letter.

372
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:28,030
It is.

373
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:30,637
The Guardian has sent us an urgent update.

374
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:31,550
The Guardian?

375
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,407
So it's a letter from Field.

376
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:34,580
No, wait.

377
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:37,546
How does it make sense
that a Field can write?

378
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:38,758
I'll read it aloud.

379
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,197
Howdy, everyone.

380
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:41,420
My name is Field.

381
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:43,717
I heard the news from Director Bear,

382
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:46,857
so I'm up to date on the
nasty little sitch you're in.

383
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:50,297
I've already spoken with the Demon Lord,
so what do you say we all work together?

384
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:52,498
to kick the Nether Lord's evil butt?

385
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:54,520
He wants to kick butt?

386
00:19:54,780 --> 00:19:57,100
That's one aggressive, um, Field.

387
00:19:57,440 --> 00:20:00,897
I've included a detailed plan of
attack along with this here letter.

388
00:20:00,980 --> 00:20:02,921
So please look it over carefully.

389
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:08,141
If you have any questions or concerns, just
jot them down and give them to Kuroyata.

390
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:12,337
Also, if you don't mind, please
show the following to Boxxo.

391
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:13,280
It's for you.

392
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:17,460
A vending machine's a weird
reincarnation, broseph.

393
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:20,247
But then again, I'm a
field, so I can't talk.

394
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:23,777
Let's have a nice long chat
about Japan when this is over.

395
00:20:23,860 --> 00:20:27,577
I'd love to share some delicious veggies,
but I know you don't have a mouth.

396
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,840
Anyway, can't wait to meet ya!

397
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:34,320
Somehow, I have the feeling I'd
really hit it off with this field guy.

398
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:38,838
Whenever we meet, I'll gift him up
with some nostalgic Japanese goods.

399
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:41,257
After that, we held a strategy meeting.

400
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:44,811
We wrote down a few suggestions
and gave them to Kuro Yada.

401
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:52,437
Burning down the forest vanquished
quite a few of our monster foes.

402
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:55,817
Even so, we may have thinned the
ranks of the low-level monsters,

403
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:59,135
but nearly all of the highly
skilled ones still remain.

404
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:00,580
It's go time.

405
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:04,217
I'll do everything within my
vending powers to support our plan.

406
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:08,065
Besides, I'll get to fight alongside
my fellow countryman field.

407
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:10,534
Just the thought of it gets me excited.

408
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:13,640
Hey, Boxo, are you excited
about something? Huh?

409
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:15,040
Is she psychic now?

410
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:16,200
How can you tell?

411
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,937
Kind of seems like he's just
standing around like usual.

412
00:21:19,020 --> 00:21:20,897
I guess you still haven't figured it out.

413
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:22,977
His lights are a dead
giveaway for when he's

414
00:21:23,060 --> 00:21:24,437
going through something or feeling happy.

415
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:29,520
Even as a vending machine, my poker face
leaves a lot to be desired. He lights up.

416
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:30,880
Pity knows that.

417
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:34,060
It's obvious, kinda. Oh, Pity.

418
00:21:34,380 --> 00:21:35,857
You're a shell-a-bad liar.

419
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:38,116
This isn't a competition or anything.

420
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,957
I've known Boxo the longest,

421
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:43,217
and I've spent the most time with
him, so I'm definitely the winner.

422
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:44,857
Then I'm the first runner-up.

423
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:46,705
Length of time doesn't matter.

424
00:21:47,020 --> 00:21:50,957
If I were a lady, this is when I'd
say, don't fight over little old me.

425
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:52,177
But I'm not, so I won't.

426
00:21:52,260 --> 00:21:55,620
Anyway, this is no time
to battle over Boxxo.

427
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:03,960
Right now, our only focus should
be kicking the Netherlord's butt!

428
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,840
Oh?

429
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:37,940
I look forward to serving you again.
